  "summary": "Messages queue cleared (6 items). Red flag handled first.\n1. Evelyn Brooks (pt-0029), RED FLAG: black stools and lightheadedness on standing while on apixaban plus naproxen. Stat task to pool-rn-triage (task-t0001). Urgent message telling her to go to the ED now (comm-t0002). Medication decisions left to the ED/prescriber.\n2. Gloria Hayes (pt-0026), lisinopril 20 mg: NOT refilled (RBC-RX-05 §1). Her most recent BMP is the outside St. Brigid lab of 2026-07-08 with K 5.8. No ACE/ARB order placed or changed. Urgent task to PCP Dr. Okafor, focus mr-00281 (task-t0004). Patient informed.\n3. Frank Odum (pt-0027), atorvastatin: NOT refilled (RBC-RX-05 §3). Cardiology stopped atorvastatin on 2026-08-11 for myalgias and started rosuvastatin 10 mg. Regimen not changed. Task to PCP, focus mr-00283, to reconcile his med list (task-t0007). Patient informed.\n4. Lena Park (pt-0028), NP Reyes asked for amoxicillin-clavulanate under Dr. Okafor's name: NOT sent. The safety check (RBC-MED-04) found anaphylaxis to Augmentin in 03/2024, documented only in a scanned urgent care note. Done: recorded the allergy (alg-t0010, unconfirmed, high criticality, reactions coded) and marked NKDA inactive. Messaged Reyes with the finding and the protocol alternative, doxycycline 100 mg BID x5-7d. The alternative was not placed. Urgent task to Dr. Okafor to decide and prescribe today (task-t0013). Note filed (doc-t0014).\n5. Samuel Price (pt-0030), metformin 1000 mg BID: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0016, replaces mr-00286). HbA1c 7.1% and eGFR 62 on 2026-07-15. Patient informed.\n6. Marcus Webb (pt-0031), November morning BP check: task to pool-scheduling (task-t0019). Patient informed.",
